    {
      "source_line": 1269,
      "literal_context": "Suppose that the given nonsymmetric graphical collection $\\calX$ with values in vector spaces is the linearisation of a nonsymmetric graphical collection $\\calU$ with values in sets; in other words, $\\calU(\\Gamma)$ is a functorial choice of a basis in $\\calX(\\Gamma)$. Then the free shuffle reconnectad $\\calN_{\\Sha}(\\calX)$ is the linearisation of the free shuffle reconnectad $\\calN_{\\Sha}(\\calU)$, and we can talk about monomials $\\calN_{\\Sha}(\\calX)$. We say that a monomial $m$ is \\emph{divisible} by another monomial $m'$ if it can be obtained from $m'$ by iteration of structure operations. A collection of total well orders of all sets $\\calN_{\\Sha}(\\calU)(\\Gamma)$ is said to be a \\emph{monomial ordering} if each structure operation of $\\calN_{\\Sha}(\\calU)$ is strictly increasing in each argument. ",
